Ezero frontend source status

Canonical original Zero source: ezero/compiler.zero, composed in order from
head, lexer, parser, expression and finish.zero.part. The compiled frontend
validates UTF-8, emits typed phrases, checked expressions, one-based list
operations, control flow, functions and source-line diagnostics.

The file extension adds create/del/watch/search/save/go/disks, read/rm aliases
and bare Zero drive paths such as A:|note. The current source is 49133 bytes.
Native file validation includes successful compilation of bare paths, aliases,
normal list separators, and rejection of wrong builtin arities.
See ../tests/files-verification.ztext for completed current results.

Historical pre-extension validation covered 522 structural/capacity/malformed
inputs and the integrated behavioral suite. Those historical results do not
certify subsequent source changes. Product checks now use the original Zero
verifier in tools/check.zero and its checks/ fixtures.
